  "meta": {
    "title": "Why Animals Don't Cross This Invisible Line 🦘🐒🚧 The Wallace Line",
    "description": "Bali and Lombok 🇮🇩 are only about 35 km apart, but their animals are completely different 🐒🦘 In 1859 naturalist Alfred Russel Wallace noticed an invisible boundary: west of it you find Asian animals like apes, elephants and monkeys, east of it Australasian ones like marsupials 🤯 Why? Deep water. Even when sea levels dropped 120 m in the Ice Age, the islands never connected Asia with Australia 🌊",
    "pinnedComment": [
      "35 km of water that animals never crossed 🤯🐒🦘",
      "Did you know about the Wallace Line? 👇",
      "Which invisible line should we explain next? 🗺️"
    ],
